<section style="padding:96px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>If you're searching for oil tank removal in Moncton, chances are you've switched heat sources or your insurance company sent you a letter about that ageing tank. Either way, you want it gone safely, without drama and without a mess in the driveway. Hub City Tank Co removes residential oil tanks across Greater Moncton and Southeast New Brunswick, and most aboveground removals run <strong>$500 to $1,500</strong>, including the line disconnect and disposal of any leftover oil.</p><p>We're licensed and insured, and we put every estimate in writing before the truck rolls. Whether your tank sits beside the house, in the basement, or you're clearing the way for a <a href="/oil-tank-replacement-moncton/">new tank</a> or a heat pump, you'll know exactly what it costs before we touch a fitting.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Handle</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">What's Included in Every Visit</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #DCE6EF;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0D2C47;margin:0 0 8px;">Honest, Written Pricing</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Most aboveground removals cost $500 to $1,500, and we put your number in writing before we start. No surprises when the job's done.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #DCE6EF;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0D2C47;margin:0 0 8px;">Line Disconnect Included</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">We cap and disconnect the fill, vent, and supply lines on every removal. It's part of the price, not an add-on.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #DCE6EF;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0D2C47;margin:0 0 8px;">Residual Oil Handled</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Whatever oil is left in the tank gets pumped out and disposed of properly. That's included too.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #DCE6EF;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0D2C47;margin:0 0 8px;">Basement Tank Experience</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Tanks in tight basements need to be drained and cut down to fit through the door. We do it cleanly for a modest extra charge.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #DCE6EF;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0D2C47;margin:0 0 8px;">OHPA Grant Friendly</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Switching from oil to a heat pump? The federal OHPA grant explicitly covers safe tank removal, and our written invoice works for your claim.</p>
